# Update SessionStart hook to surface latest handoff doc

**Status:** PENDING — execute in a DeepSeek (coding-mode) session.

## 1. Scope

Update `backend-session-start.ps1` so that when launching in PLANNING mode it automatically
finds the latest `docs/handoff/*.md` in the current project directory and injects its contents
into the session context. This way planning-mode Claude immediately knows what was built last
session without the user having to point to the file manually.

## 2. Files to change

- `C:/Users/User/.claude/hooks/backend-session-start.ps1` — add handoff doc lookup to the planning-mode branch.

## 3. Exact changes

Replace the current planning-mode `$policy` block with the version below. The new code:
1. Looks for `docs/handoff/*.md` in the current working directory.
2. If found, reads the most recently modified one.
3. Appends its contents to the context injected into the session.

```powershell
# Replace the existing planning-mode block (the else branch) with:

} else {
    $mode = 'PLANNING'
    $backend = 'Anthropic (Opus or other Claude model)'
    $policy = @"
Mode: PLANNING (Anthropic backend)
You MUST NOT: edit source code files. The PreToolUse hook will hard-block Write/Edit on non-.md files.
You SHOULD: produce technical change specifications as Markdown files under docs/changes/<short-name>.md. Each spec must include:
  1. Scope: one-paragraph summary of the change.
  2. Files to change: full paths.
  3. Exact changes: code-level detail (signatures, new functions, modifications). Pseudocode or full snippets.
  4. Acceptance criteria: how to verify it works.
  5. Commands to run: build, test, lint.
  6. Risks / open questions.
A later DeepSeek session will execute these specs.

At the START of this session:
  - Summarise the latest handoff doc (injected below) back to the user.
  - List any pending specs in docs/changes/ and ask which to focus on.
"@

    # Look for the latest handoff doc in the current project
    $handoffDir = Join-Path (Get-Location) 'docs/handoff'
    $handoffContent = ''
    if (Test-Path $handoffDir) {
        $latest = Get-ChildItem $handoffDir -Filter '*.md' | Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1
        if ($latest) {
            $handoffContent = "`n`n---`n## Latest handoff doc: $($latest.Name)`n`n" + (Get-Content $latest.FullName -Raw)
        }
    }
    if (-not $handoffContent) {
        $handoffContent = "`n`n---`n## No handoff doc found`nThis appears to be a new project or the first planning session. No prior build context available."
    }
}
```

The final `$ctx` line stays the same:
```powershell
$ctx = "## Active LLM backend: $backend`n## ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL: $url`n`n$policy$handoffContent"
```

Make sure `$handoffContent` is declared before the if/else so it's in scope for both branches (set it to `''` at the top of the script).

## 4. Acceptance criteria

1. In a project that has `docs/handoff/2024-01-15.md`, launch `planning-mode`. The SessionStart context injected should include the contents of that file.
2. In a project with no `docs/handoff/` folder, launch `planning-mode`. The context should say "No handoff doc found."
3. In a coding-mode session, the handoff lookup does not run (only planning-mode branch executes it).

